{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-82054","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-146063","text":"locu.systems"}]},{"id":"blk-82055","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146064","marks":["bold"],"text":"Direction, ruled 2026-09-14: a host for ComputeDriven loci"},{"id":"spn-146065","text":" — a locus is what the customer deploys and is billed for, a carrier is the rented machine under it, and the meter counts admitted transitions. Record: "},{"id":"spn-146066","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/90_LOCUS_HOSTING.md"},{"id":"spn-146067","text":". "},{"id":"spn-146068","marks":["bold"],"text":"Nothing in it is built."},{"id":"spn-146069","text":" "},{"id":"spn-146070","marks":["code"],"text":"80_SERVICE_MANAGEMENT_PILOT.md"},{"id":"spn-146071","text":" is the superseded direction from earlier the same day, banded rather than rewritten."}]},{"id":"blk-82056","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146072","marks":["bold"],"text":"The domain is new; the repository, this directory and the nav property key are not renamed."},{"id":"spn-146073","text":" The shared nav still renders the previous name; the page declares that disagreement and the gate refuses to publish while it is undeclared. Do not edit "},{"id":"spn-146074","marks":["code"],"text":"amp-nav.js"},{"id":"spn-146075","text":" to fix it — that file belongs to lane N."}]},{"id":"blk-82057","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146076","text":"What is in the tree from the abandoned agent-deployment direction: a Postgres schema and edge functions in the sibling "},{"id":"spn-146077","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand-supabase/"},{"id":"spn-146078","text":", and a Vite/React/TypeScript dashboard against a Supabase client. "},{"id":"spn-146079","marks":["bold"],"text":"It does not execute an agent on a runtime."}]},{"id":"blk-82058","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-146080","text":"What is here"}]},{"id":"blk-82059","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"index.html          the marketing page — GENERATED, see below\n_redirects          sends old_scrap/, src/ and apps/ away from the live host (SHELL.md r14)\nconsole/            the PHASE-TWO CONSOLE PROTOTYPE, served at /console/ — hand-authored, not generated\nsrc/                the marketing page's template, stylesheet and two scripts\nrecords/            the frozen records the page is generated from\nbuild-site.mjs      emits index.html, boot.js, say.js\nlaunch-gate.mjs     reads the artifact and refuses to publish a page that lies\napps/web/           the dashboard — Vite + React + TypeScript, Supabase client\ndocs/spec/          the v1 specification set, part of it superseded\namp-nav.js          portfolio nav, a DEPLOYED copy — do not edit it here\nold_scrap/          previous versions, historical, not authoritative"},{"id":"blk-82060","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146081","marks":["code"],"text":"package.json"},{"id":"spn-146082","text":" declares npm workspaces at "},{"id":"spn-146083","marks":["code"],"text":"apps/*"},{"id":"spn-146084","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-146085","marks":["code"],"text":"packages/*"},{"id":"spn-146086","text":". There is one workspace, "},{"id":"spn-146087","marks":["code"],"text":"apps/web"},{"id":"spn-146088","text":". "},{"id":"spn-146089","marks":["bold"],"text":"`packages/` does not exist"},{"id":"spn-146090","text":", so there is no SDK and no CLI, and the marketing page says so with a probe that re-checks it on every build."}]},{"id":"blk-82061","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146091","text":"The edge functions and migrations this product runs on are "},{"id":"spn-146092","marks":["bold"],"text":"not in this repository"},{"id":"spn-146093","text":". They live in the sibling "},{"id":"spn-146094","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand-supabase/"},{"id":"spn-146095","text":" repo, under "},{"id":"spn-146096","marks":["code"],"text":"functions/webhost-*"},{"id":"spn-146097","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-146098","marks":["code"],"text":"migrations/*webhost*"},{"id":"spn-146099","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-82062","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-146100","text":"The marketing page is GENERATED. Do not hand-edit "},{"id":"spn-146101","marks":["code"],"text":"index.html"},{"id":"spn-146102","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-82063","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146103","marks":["code"],"text":"/index.html"},{"id":"spn-146104","text":", "},{"id":"spn-146105","marks":["code"],"text":"/boot.js"},{"id":"spn-146106","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-146107","marks":["code"],"text":"/say.js"},{"id":"spn-146108","text":" are emitted by "},{"id":"spn-146109","marks":["code"],"text":"build-site.mjs"},{"id":"spn-146110","text":" from "},{"id":"spn-146111","marks":["code"],"text":"records/surface.json"},{"id":"spn-146112","text":", "},{"id":"spn-146113","marks":["code"],"text":"records/evidence.json"},{"id":"spn-146114","text":", "},{"id":"spn-146115","marks":["code"],"text":"src/landing.html"},{"id":"spn-146116","text":", "},{"id":"spn-146117","marks":["code"],"text":"src/shell.css"},{"id":"spn-146118","text":", "},{"id":"spn-146119","marks":["code"],"text":"src/boot.js"},{"id":"spn-146120","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-146121","marks":["code"],"text":"src/say.js"},{"id":"spn-146122","text":". "},{"id":"spn-146123","marks":["bold"],"text":"An edit to the served HTML is silently reverted by the next build."},{"id":"spn-146124","text":" Change the record or the template."}]},{"id":"blk-82064","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"npm run site:launch   # emit the page, then prove it"},{"id":"blk-82065","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146125","marks":["code"],"text":"launch-gate.mjs"},{"id":"spn-146126","text":" reads the emitted artifact and refuses to publish when it and the records disagree — a retracted claim reinstated (anywhere, including inside a comment or an attribute), a rung invented, a call to action the rung has not earned, a hand-typed count, a cited source line that has stopped saying what it is quoted as saying, a "},{"id":"spn-146127","marks":["code"],"text":"mailto:"},{"id":"spn-146128","text":", a text token below 4.5:1, a button whose colour is decided by a non-button rule, an artifact that is not what its source compiles to, or an animation constant leaking into the copy. The gate prints its own total; "},{"id":"spn-146129","marks":["bold"],"text":"do not hand-type a check count anywhere"},{"id":"spn-146130","text":", that is how the published and printed numbers drift apart."}]},{"id":"blk-82066","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146131","text":"Most of the page's claims are NEGATIVE — \"there is no AWS dependency\", \"nothing reads an "},{"id":"spn-146132","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-146133","text":"\", \""},{"id":"spn-146134","marks":["code"],"text":"packages/"},{"id":"spn-146135","text":" does not exist\". Those are the ones the build re-derives off disk on every run, because nobody edits a sentence on a marketing page when they add a dependency."}]},{"id":"blk-82067","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146136","text":"**The three "},{"id":"spn-146137","marks":["code"],"text":"site:*"},{"id":"spn-146138","text":" scripts are deliberately not wired into "},{"id":"spn-146139","marks":["code"],"text":"build"},{"id":"spn-146140","text":", "},{"id":"spn-146141","marks":["code"],"text":"dev"},{"id":"spn-146142","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-146143","marks":["code"],"text":"test"},{"id":"spn-146144","text":".** Those belong to "},{"id":"spn-146145","marks":["code"],"text":"apps/web"},{"id":"spn-146146","text":", which is a separate artifact with a separate toolchain. Do not entangle them."}]},{"id":"blk-82068","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-146147","text":"ONE PAGE. The site and the console share a document and a URL space."}]},{"id":"blk-82069","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146148","text":"There is no second site. "},{"id":"spn-146149","marks":["code"],"text":"/"},{"id":"spn-146150","text":" serves the home view; "},{"id":"spn-146151","marks":["code"],"text":"#/ops/*"},{"id":"spn-146152","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-146153","marks":["code"],"text":"#/account/*"},{"id":"spn-146154","text":" are the operator console and the client portal, rendered by "},{"id":"spn-146155","marks":["code"],"text":"/app.js"},{"id":"spn-146156","text":" into "},{"id":"spn-146157","marks":["code"],"text":"#app"},{"id":"spn-146158","text":". Three rules hold that together and all three are checked:"}]},{"id":"blk-82070","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-82072","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146159","marks":["bold"],"text":"The home view is in the served bytes."},{"id":"spn-146160","text":" "},{"id":"spn-146161","marks":["code"],"text":"build-site.mjs"},{"id":"spn-146162","text":" generates it into"}]}],"id":"blk-82071","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-82073","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146163","marks":["code"],"text":"#home"},{"id":"spn-146164","text":" from the frozen records. "},{"id":"spn-146165","marks":["code"],"text":"/app.js"},{"id":"spn-146166","text":" may show or hide it and may "},{"id":"spn-146167","marks":["bold"],"text":"never author it"},{"id":"spn-146168","text":" — §3c deletes every script and the empty "},{"id":"spn-146169","marks":["code"],"text":"#app"},{"id":"spn-146170","text":" from the artifact and requires each text node a reader sees to survive. A price, a status or a count migrating into the script is refused there."}]},{"id":"blk-82074","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-82076","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146171","marks":["bold"],"text":"`src/app.css` is scoped to `#app`."},{"id":"spn-146172","text":" It shares "},{"id":"spn-146173","marks":["code"],"text":".btn"},{"id":"spn-146174","text":", "},{"id":"spn-146175","marks":["code"],"text":".tag"},{"id":"spn-146176","text":", "},{"id":"spn-146177","marks":["code"],"text":".status"},{"id":"spn-146178","text":","}]}],"id":"blk-82075","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-82077","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146179","marks":["code"],"text":".card"},{"id":"spn-146180","text":" and bare "},{"id":"spn-146181","marks":["code"],"text":"table"},{"id":"spn-146182","text":" rules with the shell for different things; unscoped it would silently restyle the page a visitor lands on. Only the overlays appended to "},{"id":"spn-146183","marks":["code"],"text":"<body>"},{"id":"spn-146184","text":" (scrim, modal, toast) are unscoped, and none of those names exists in the shell. The gate enumerates every rule."}]},{"id":"blk-82078","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-82080","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146185","marks":["bold"],"text":"The palette is not its own."},{"id":"spn-146186","text":" Every colour name in "},{"id":"spn-146187","marks":["code"],"text":"app.css"},{"id":"spn-146188","text":" is an alias of"}]}],"id":"blk-82079","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-82081","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146189","text":"the shell token carrying that role, so one palette paints both halves. Only "},{"id":"spn-146190","marks":["code"],"text":"--util"},{"id":"spn-146191","text":", "},{"id":"spn-146192","marks":["code"],"text":"--alarm"},{"id":"spn-146193","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-146194","marks":["code"],"text":"--indet"},{"id":"spn-146195","text":" are new, and "},{"id":"spn-146196","marks":["code"],"text":"--util"},{"id":"spn-146197","text":" must never be the accent: the argument of the site is that one of those two numbers is louder than the other for a reason."}]},{"id":"blk-82082","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146198","marks":["bold"],"text":"The standing notice"},{"id":"spn-146199","text":" carries "},{"id":"spn-146200","marks":["code"],"text":"data-prototype"},{"id":"spn-146201","text":" and must sit outside "},{"id":"spn-146202","marks":["code"],"text":"#app"},{"id":"spn-146203","text":", because a notice the panel paints disappears the moment the panel throws. The panel's fleet is invented and "},{"id":"spn-146204","marks":["bold"],"text":"its figures may not be repeated anywhere"},{"id":"spn-146205","text":" until a kernel counts admitted transitions under load."}]},{"id":"blk-82083","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-146206","text":"Source-of-truth spec"}]},{"id":"blk-82084","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-82086","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146207","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/00_MASTER_SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-146208","text":" — master engineering spec"}]}],"id":"blk-82085","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-82088","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146209","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/10_API_CONTRACTS.md"},{"id":"spn-146210","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-146211","marks":["code"],"text":"20_RUNTIME_PROVIDER_INTERFACE.md"},{"id":"spn-146212","text":" ·"}]}],"id":"blk-82087","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-82089","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146213","marks":["code"],"text":"30_DATA_MODEL_SUPABASE.md"},{"id":"spn-146214","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-146215","marks":["code"],"text":"40_SECURITY_SECRETS_COMPLIANCE.md"},{"id":"spn-146216","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-146217","marks":["code"],"text":"50_OBSERVABILITY_BILLING_LIMITS.md"},{"id":"spn-146218","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-146219","marks":["code"],"text":"60_TESTING_ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"id":"spn-146220","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-146221","marks":["code"],"text":"70_AMPERSAND_PROTOCOL_INTEGRATION.md"}]},{"id":"blk-82090","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-82092","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146222","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/80_SERVICE_MANAGEMENT_PILOT.md"},{"id":"spn-146223","text":" — the current direction and first pilot; read it first"}]}],"id":"blk-82091","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-82094","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146224","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/adr/"},{"id":"spn-146225","text":" — architecture decision records"}]}],"id":"blk-82093","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-82096","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146226","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/progress/"},{"id":"spn-146227","text":" — implementation progress logs"}]}],"id":"blk-82095","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-82098","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146228","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/REALIGNMENT_PLAN.md"}]}],"id":"blk-82097","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-82099","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146229","text":"Read the master spec before implementing features, "},{"id":"spn-146230","marks":["bold"],"text":"and read its supersession banner first"},{"id":"spn-146231","text":": the data-layer half of the spec set is superseded. See README.md."}]},{"id":"blk-82100","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-146232","text":"[&] Protocol integration — specified, not implemented"}]},{"id":"blk-82101","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146233","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/spec/70_AMPERSAND_PROTOCOL_INTEGRATION.md"},{"id":"spn-146234","text":" describes "},{"id":"spn-146235","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-146236","text":" manifest support, MCP sidecar orchestration, agent-to-agent routing and Delegatic governance enforcement. "},{"id":"spn-146237","marks":["bold"],"text":"None of it is built."},{"id":"spn-146238","text":" No code in this repository or in the sibling edge functions reads an "},{"id":"spn-146239","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-146240","text":"; the build counts the source files that so much as mention one, and the count is zero."}]},{"id":"blk-82102","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-146241","text":"Build and test"}]},{"id":"blk-82103","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"npm install\nnpm run dev            # Vite dev server for apps/web\nnpm test               # vitest across workspaces\nnpm run typecheck\nnpm run lint\nnpm run format:check\nnpm run site:launch    # the marketing page: emit, then prove"},{"id":"blk-82104","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-146242","text":"Constraints"}]},{"id":"blk-82105","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-82107","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146243","text":"Node >= 20"}]}],"id":"blk-82106","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-82109","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146244","text":"TypeScript strict mode; ESLint + Prettier enforced"}]}],"id":"blk-82108","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-82111","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146245","text":"Never commit secrets. "},{"id":"spn-146246","marks":["code"],"text":"apps/web/env.example"},{"id":"spn-146247","text":" shows the shape."}]}],"id":"blk-82110","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-82113","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-146248","marks":["bold"],"text":"Do not add a dependency to make a marketing claim true — fix the claim."}]}],"id":"blk-82112","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierazi25ewhenycownoq6wuz34uvy65nke2wa3lqv4a7p3buly6tania","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}